msgid "Gods, he was beautiful."
msgstr "Боги, он был прекрасен."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "Gods, how can I deny this poor girl?"
msgstr "Боги, как я могу отказать этой бедной девочке?"

#. emotion: Surprised incredulity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, how did one even put one of these one."
msgstr "Боги, как вообще надевают такое?"

#. emotion: With surprised bewilderment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, how had she ended up here..."
msgstr "Боги, как она вообще здесь оказалась..."

#. emotion: Inquisitively puzzled, with an undertone of bewilderment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, how had she ended up here? How quickly had her life turned about..."
msgstr "Боги, как она здесь оказалась? Как быстро перевернулась её жизнь..."

#. emotion: With a somber, urgent tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, if half of what she had heard tonight was even true, the world might very well be ending."
msgstr "Боги, если хотя бы половина того, что она услышала сегодня, правда, мир вполне мог быть на грани конца."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods, is this what men have to deal with all the time?"
msgstr "Боги, и с этим мужчинам приходится иметь дело постоянно?"

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, it felt so long ago."
msgstr "Боги, кажется, это было так давно."

#. emotion: Reflectively self-aware
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods, just look at you."
msgstr "Боги, только посмотри на себя."

#. emotion: Reflectively thoughtful
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, just look at you. You look like the spittin image of my wife when she was your age."
msgstr "Боги, ты только посмотри на себя. Вылитая моя жена в молодости."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "Gods, knew you were worth the trouble."
msgstr "Боги, знал, что ты того стоишь."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Mayor"
msgid "Gods, last time we send every last man, even those young lads that can barely be called men, into the forest."
msgstr "Боги, в последний раз мы послали каждого мужчину, даже тех юнцов, которых едва можно назвать мужчинами, в лес."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Gods, listen to be blather. This wine...truly, perhaps we should reschedule."
msgstr "Боги, послушай, что я болтаю. Это вино... правда, возможно, нам стоит перенести встречу."

#. emotion: Solemn regret
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods, now I'm sorry I even asked. I didn't mean to spoil the surprise."
msgstr "Боги, теперь мне жаль, что я спросила. Я не хотела портить сюрприз."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Gods, perhaps I should take up soldiering. It works wonders on the body."
msgstr "Боги, может, мне тоже заняться военным делом. Оно творит чудеса с телом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods, please, more!"
msgstr "Боги, пожалуйста, ещё!"

#. emotion: Tense anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she could smell the alcohol on them from here."
msgstr "Боги, она чувствовала запах алкоголя от них даже отсюда."

#. emotion: Bitterly regretful sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she cursed herself for having allowed it."
msgstr "Боги, она проклинала себя за то, что позволила этому случиться."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she hoped not."
msgstr "Боги, она надеялась, что нет."

#. emotion: Intrigued and hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she realized..."
msgstr "Боги, она поняла..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she thought to herself."
msgstr "Боги, подумала она."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she thought, why did this turn her on so much."
msgstr "Боги, думала она, почему это так её заводит."

#. emotion: In a reflective, slightly awestruck tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she thought. He's announcing it, as if she was some prize."
msgstr "Боги, подумала она. Он объявляет об этом, словно она какой-то приз."

#. emotion: Tenderly lamenting, with a hint of sadness
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she was so weak for them. If only they knew how easily they played on her heart."
msgstr "Боги, она была так слаба к ним. Если бы они только знали, как легко они играют на её сердце."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, she wondered. How had she been so foolish in following that voice."
msgstr "Боги, гадала она. Как она могла быть так глупа, последовав за этим голосом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, that mouth of yours..."
msgstr "Боги, этот твой рот..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Gods, that will be a story, no?"
msgstr "Боги, вот это будет история, не так ли?"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Gods, that's a story if ever I heard some."
msgstr "Боги, вот это история, если я когда-либо слышал."

#. emotion: Contentedly smiling
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Gods, that's good."
msgstr "Боги, как хорошо."

#. emotion: Sarcastically praising
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "Gods, the bribes I've paid out alone would buy me a few more mansions."
msgstr "Боги, одни взятки, которые я заплатил, могли бы купить мне ещё несколько особняков."

#. emotion: Surprised admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "Gods, the girl can drink. Who knew, you looked so uptight with your clothes on."
msgstr "Боги, девчонка умеет пить. Кто бы мог подумать, ты выглядела такой зажатой в одежде."

#. emotion: Concerned and apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Gods, the hour...I fear that I have taken up too much of your time."
msgstr "Боги, час... боюсь, я занял слишком много вашего времени."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, the quality of people that I get these days..."
msgstr "Боги, что за люди ко мне приходят в последнее время..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, the things she would do for him. The ways in which she would offer herself up to him."
msgstr "Боги, что бы она сделала для него. Как бы она предложила себя ему."

#. emotion: Disapprovingly disbelieving
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Gods, the two of you break easy."
msgstr "Боги, вы двое легко ломаетесь."

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Gods, there isn't even anyone here besides me and you still act like this."
msgstr "Боги, здесь же никого нет, кроме меня, а ты всё ещё ведёшь себя так."

#. emotion: Intrigued reverence
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Gods, there was no single place in all the world more drowned in Divine energy."
msgstr "Боги, не было во всём мире места, более пропитанного Божественной энергией."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Other man"
msgid "Gods, thought I'd had shit luck all day, but things lookin up."
msgstr "Боги, думал, весь день не везёт, но дела налаживаются."

#. emotion: Somberly reflecting
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, to think I was almost done with life."
msgstr "Боги, подумать только — я почти простился с жизнью."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Gods, today was supposed to be an easy day. It sure went sideways fast."
msgstr "Боги, сегодняшний день должен был быть лёгким. Но всё быстро пошло наперекосяк."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, what I've done to deserve a beauty like yours..."
msgstr "Боги, что я сделал, чтобы заслужить такую красавицу, как ты..."

#. emotion: Intrigued and thoughtful whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, what had she been thinking, going along with this man."
msgstr "Боги, о чём она думала, соглашаясь на это с этим человеком."

#. emotion: Contemplatively questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, what if that was her fate? Sarah knew more clearly than ever that she had to escape."
msgstr "Боги, что, если это её судьба? Сара знала яснее, чем когда-либо — она должна сбежать."

#. emotion: Anxiously curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, what she had allowed that man to do to her..."
msgstr "Боги, что она позволила этому мужчине с собой сделать..."

#. emotion: Surprised and questioning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, what was she doing with a man of his age."
msgstr "Боги, что она делала с мужчиной его возраста."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods, why could she have been so foolish as to reach out to the voice? Had she not been warned?"
msgstr "Боги, почему она была так глупа, что откликнулась на голос? Разве её не предупреждали?"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Gods, you always lucky, huh? Go for a piss and you fish out a lass like that?"
msgstr "Боги, ты вечно везучий, а? Пошёл отлить и выловил такую тёлку?"

#. emotion: Disappointedly weary
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Gods, you can be obnoxious."
msgstr "Боги, ты бываешь невыносимой."

#. emotion: Admiringly speaking
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Gods, you have no idea how lucky you got."
msgstr "Боги, ты не представляешь, как тебе повезло."

#. emotion: Warily whispering
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods, you really are terrible, aren't you?"
msgstr "Боги, ты действительно ужасна, да?"

#. emotion: Stern disappointment
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "Gods, you seemed like such a fun girl, and now you're causing me a headache."
msgstr "Боги, ты казалась такой весёлой девушкой, а теперь у меня от тебя голова болит."

#. emotion: Somberly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Gods, you'll be the end of me."
msgstr "Боги, ты меня в могилу сведёшь."

#. emotion: Playfully teasing
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods, you're a good fuck."
msgstr "Боги, с тобой хорошо трахаться."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Gods, you're beautiful."
msgstr "Боги, ты прекрасна."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Gods, you're beautiful..."
msgstr "Боги, ты прекрасна..."

#. emotion: In a low menacing whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods, you're lucky you've got a body like this or I'd have been done with you long ago."
msgstr "Боги, тебе повезло, что у тебя такое тело, иначе я бы давно с тобой покончил."

#. emotion: In a contemplative, slightly reproachful tone
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods, you're pathetic."
msgstr "Боги, ты жалка."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods, you're so predictable."
msgstr "Боги, ты такой предсказуемый."

#. emotion: Tenderly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Gods, your beautiful..."
msgstr "Боги, ты прекрасна..."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods."
msgstr "Боги."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods."
msgstr "Боги."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Confused and bewildered
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Gods..."
msgstr "Боги..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Gods...Gabriel..."
msgstr "Боги... Габриэль..."

#. emotion: Sorrowful longing
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Gods...I envy you, Sarah."
msgstr "Боги... я завидую тебе, Сара."

#. emotion: In a low, almost pleading tone
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Gods...I must be a terrible huntsman not to hear you sneaking up on me."
msgstr "Боги... я, должно быть, ужасный охотник, раз не услышал, как ты подкрадываешься."

#. emotion: In a stunned, awestruck whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Duke Antonio"
msgid "Gods...I still can't believe this is real..."
msgstr "Боги... я всё ещё не могу поверить, что это настоящее..."

#. emotion: Annoyedly pleading
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Gods...don't make me wait any longer!"
msgstr "Боги... не заставляйте меня ждать дольше!"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods...he read much. So much, all the time..."
msgstr "Боги... он так много читал. Всё время, постоянно..."

#. emotion: In a somber, contemplative tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods...it's cold..."
msgstr "Боги… как холодно…"

#. emotion: Thoughtfully contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods...she thought to herself."
msgstr "Боги... — подумала она про себя."

#. emotion: Detached curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods...that..."
msgstr "Боги... это..."

#. emotion: Thoughtfully bemused
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Gods...time is a strange thing here."
msgstr "Боги... время здесь странное."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Gods...what did I do to deserve you..."
msgstr "Боги... что я сделал, чтобы заслужить тебя..."

#. emotion: In a somber, reflective tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods...what madness had overtaken her."
msgstr "Боги... какое безумие на неё нашло."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods...what time is it..."
msgstr "Боги...сколько времени..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Gods...when did this happen."
msgstr "Боги...когда это случилось."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Gods...whenever I look in your face it's like I can see hints of him."
msgstr "Боги... каждый раз, когда я смотрю на твоё лицо, я словно вижу в нём его черты."

#. emotion: Pensively intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Garret"
msgid "Gods...where do I even begin."
msgstr "Боги...с чего же мне начать."

#. emotion: Reflectively puzzled
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gods...why her?"
msgstr "Боги... почему она?"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Gods...you'll probably even be good at that too."
msgstr "Боги... ты, вероятно, даже будешь в этом хороша."

#. emotion: Somberly intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Gods...you're so easy to talk to."
msgstr "Боги...с тобой так легко говорить."

#. emotion: Confidently assured
msgctxt "speaker:Gideon"
msgid "Goes to show how well I know you..."
msgstr "Показывает, как хорошо я тебя знаю..."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Goes to show you what I get for bein such a good person."
msgstr "Вот что я получаю за то, что я такой хороший человек."

#. emotion: In a studiously attentive manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Going through the documents, Sarah tried to make sense of them."
msgstr "Просматривая документы, Сара пыталась в них разобраться."

#. emotion: Contentedly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Going to school, taking on trades, eventually forming families of their own."
msgstr "Ходили в школу, обучались ремёслам, со временем создавали свои семьи."

#. emotion: Disappointedly sarcastic
msgctxt "speaker:Jasmine"
msgid "Going to war with everyone is a good recipe to lose."
msgstr "Воевать со всеми — верный способ проиграть."

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Going with Sakar to that clearing in the forest. Staying with him as he touched himself..."
msgstr "Прогулка с Сакаром к той поляне в лесу. Она осталась с ним, пока он касался себя..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gold and jewels glittered, casually strewn across the room."
msgstr "Золото и драгоценности сверкали, небрежно разбросанные по комнате."

#. emotion: In awe, with reverence
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "Gold, jewels, horses. The wealth of empires has been laid before at my feet."
msgstr "Золото, драгоценности, лошади. Богатства империй были брошены к моим ногам."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:King-On-The-Outside"
msgid "Golden soul. Star-crowned. Sarah Rose."
msgstr "Золотая душа. Увенчанная звездой. Сара Роуз."

#. emotion: Fiercely determined
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone was any hesitation, gone was any restraint."
msgstr "Не осталось ни колебаний, ни сдержанности."

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone was the labored breathing and the exhausted broken speech. The girl was as she had always been."
msgstr "Исчезли тяжёлое дыхание и усталая прерывистая речь. Девушка была такой, какой была всегда."

#. emotion: Melancholic relief
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone was the slow denying pace from before."
msgstr "Медленный, отказывающий темп исчез."

#. emotion: Calmly assured
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone were all the small signs of her awkwardness and nervousness."
msgstr "Исчезли все малейшие признаки неловкости и нервозности."

#. emotion: Reflectively nostalgic
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone were the days of pretend or feigned modesty."
msgstr "Прошли дни притворства или показной скромности."

#. emotion: With a hopeful sigh
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone were the endless days of boredom, and in their place, the highs of the dreamstalk and the lows of its absence."
msgstr "Бесконечные дни скуки исчезли, сменившись взлётами снотворца и падениями в его отсутствие."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone were the heavy grunts, now replaced with the soft moans that more closely resembled that of a woman."
msgstr "Тяжёлые хрипы исчезли, сменившись мягкими стонами, больше похожими на женские."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone were the soft and stifled moans, now instead the cries of pleasure with abandon."
msgstr "Мягкие и приглушённые стоны исчезли, теперь вместо них — крики удовольствия без удержу."

#. emotion: Sternly recalling
msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Gone were their days of studies and scholastic pursuit. Instead, they were now simply weapons of war. Valuable ones at that."
msgstr "Канули в прошлое их дни учёбы и научных изысканий. Теперь они были просто оружием войны. Причём ценным."

#. emotion: With wary anticipation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Gone, the tyranny of the Tribesmen."
msgstr "Прочь, тирания Племенников."

#. emotion: Somberly resigned
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Gonna be at least a week more of this."
msgstr "Ещё как минимум неделя этого."

#. emotion: Tenderly reminiscing, fondly hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Gonna miss ya, blondie. We had some fun."
msgstr "Буду скучать по тебе, блондиночка. Мы повеселились."

#. emotion: Nodding appreciatively
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good boy."
msgstr "Хороший мальчик."

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Dio"
msgid "Good business is settled by good food. I fear this bread must suffice for now, until our finances improve."
msgstr "Хорошее дело скрепляется хорошей едой. Боюсь, пока придётся обойтись этим хлебом, пока наши финансы не поправятся."

#. emotion: In a calm, assured tone
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Good business partners rarely make conflict."
msgstr "Хорошие деловые партнёры редко создают конфликты."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good day, sir."
msgstr "Добрый день, сударь."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good education I suppose, captain."
msgstr "Хорошее образование, полагаю, капитан."

#. emotion: Slightly impressed, contemplative
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good enough to consider, at least."
msgstr "Достаточно хорошее, чтобы рассмотреть, по крайней мере."

#. emotion: Welcomingly with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Maeiv"
msgid "Good evening, Sarah."
msgstr "Добрый вечер, Сара."

#. emotion: Reflectively amused
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good for my purse, less good on my other parts."
msgstr "Хорошо для моего кошелька, не так хорошо для других моих частей."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Good fortunes, she thought to herself. She hoped it would stay this way."
msgstr "К добру, подумала она про себя. Она надеялась, что так и останется."

#. emotion: Admiringly acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good girl, I knew you were smart."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка, я знал, что ты умная."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Guard"
msgid "Good girl, smarter than you look."
msgstr "Умница, умнее, чем кажешься."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "Good girl."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "Good girl. See, I trust ya."
msgstr "Умница. Видишь, я тебе верю."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good girl..."
msgstr "Хорошая девочка..."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Gabriel"
msgid "Good idea. Better that we get some rest. We don't want to walk into an Orc trap unprepared."
msgstr "Хорошая мысль. Лучше отдохнуть. Не хватало ещё попасть в ловушку орков неподготовленными."

#. emotion: Encouragingly with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good job girls."
msgstr "Хорошая работа, девочки."

#. emotion: Warmly, with appreciation
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good job."
msgstr "Хорошая работа."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Good man. Honest man. Well respected about town."
msgstr "Хороший человек. Честный человек. Уважаемый в городе."

#. emotion: Warily reciting
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Good men had died for no reason, other than an arrogant man's vanity."
msgstr "Хорошие люди погибли ни за что — лишь из-за тщеславия высокомерного человека."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good men."
msgstr "Хорошие люди."

#. emotion: In a friendly and affectionate greeting
msgctxt "speaker:Innkeeper"
msgid "Good mornin there."
msgstr "Доброе утречко."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Good morning to you too, Sarah."
msgstr "Доброе утро и тебе, Сара."

#. emotion: Energetically greeting
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Good morning."
msgstr "Доброе утро."

#. emotion: Energetically greeting
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Good morning."
msgstr "Доброе утро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Good news for you, it's not going to last for very long."
msgstr "Хорошая новость для тебя: это ненадолго."

#. emotion: Nodding pleasantly, with warmth
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good night to you as well, Edmond."
msgstr "Доброй ночи и вам, Эдмонд."

#. emotion: Softly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good night, Samayra."
msgstr "Спокойной ночи, Самайра."

#. emotion: Calmly good night
msgctxt "speaker:Marshal Edmond"
msgid "Good night, Sarah."
msgstr "Доброй ночи, Сара."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good night."
msgstr "Доброй ночи."

#. emotion: Contentedly reminiscing
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Good old William was a proper man of the people even back then. Ran a small little construction company."
msgstr "Добрый старый Уильям был настоящим человеком из народа даже тогда. Управлял маленькой строительной компанией."

#. emotion: Cautiously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good people are worth their weight in gold."
msgstr "Хорошие люди на вес золота."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good person?"
msgstr "Хороший человек?"

#. emotion: Somber reflection
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Good soldiers dying is always a tragedy."
msgstr "Смерть хороших солдат — всегда трагедия."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good that I got to you while you can still speak and stand up straight."
msgstr "Хорошо, что я застала тебя, пока ты ещё можешь говорить и стоять прямо."

#. emotion: Satisfiedly nodding
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Good that he carried the message though."
msgstr "Хорошо, что он передал сообщение."

#. emotion: Affectionately acknowledging
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good that you mentioned it."
msgstr "Хорошо, что ты упомянул об этом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good thing I come with no ill intentions then."
msgstr "Хорошо, что я пришла без дурных намерений."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good thing I have you."
msgstr "Хорошо, что вы со мной."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good thing you can keep your guard up for the both of us then."
msgstr "Хорошо, что ты можешь быть начеку за нас обоих."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good thing you got me lookin out for you, showin you what the real world is like."
msgstr "Хорошо, что я присматриваю за тобой и показываю тебе, каков реальный мир."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Dio"
msgid "Good thing you had me, then."
msgstr "Хорошо, что у тебя была я."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Good thing you have me as a guide then."
msgstr "Хорошо, что я у тебя есть в качестве проводника."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Elsa"
msgid "Good thing you made it here though."
msgstr "Хорошо, что ты всё-таки добралась."

#. emotion: Sardonically amused
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good thing your tits are big enough, blondie."
msgstr "Хорошо, что твои сиськи достаточно большие, блондиночка."

#. emotion: With warmth, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good thinking."
msgstr "Хорошая мысль."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:City Official"
msgid "Good to see you again old friend."
msgstr "Рад снова видеть тебя, старый друг."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good to see you again, Lord Edmond."
msgstr "Рада видеть вас снова, лорд Эдмонд."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Varga"
msgid "Good to see you as well, Marion."
msgstr "Рад вас видеть тоже, Марион."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good to see you, Marion. I hope your travels went well."
msgstr "Рады видеть тебя, Марион. Надеюсь, путешествие прошло хорошо."

#. emotion: Intrigued yet cautious whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Good was perhaps not the right word, as it was the shady ramshackle appearance of the place that drew her to it."
msgstr "«Подходящим» — пожалуй, не то слово. Её привлёк подозрительный, полуразвалившийся вид этого места."

#. emotion: In an amused, teasing tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good work blondie. Sorry bout usin you for the whole show and everything, I had to teach the kid a lesson."
msgstr "Хорошая работа, блондиночка. Прости, что использовал тебя для всего этого представления, мне нужно было проучить парня."

#. emotion: Admirative admiration
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good work today, blondie."
msgstr "Хорошая работа сегодня, Блонди."

#. emotion: Frustrated exclamation
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Good work. Rip this apart!"
msgstr "Отлично. Разорвите это!"

#. emotion: Excitedly, with enthusiasm
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "Good! Good!"
msgstr "Хорошо! Хорошо!"

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Dalia"
msgid "Good! Now, let's get you dressed up."
msgstr "Хорошо! Теперь давай оденем тебя."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, I knew you would."
msgstr "Хорошо, я знал, что ты помнишь."

#. emotion: With amused curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Good, I'll go left, you take right."
msgstr "Отлично, я пойду налево, ты — направо."

#. emotion: Warmly, with encouragement
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Good, I'm glad to hear that."
msgstr "Хорошо, рад это слышать."

#. emotion: Confused, uncertain whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Old Tribesman"
msgid "Good, because there is the issue of your...sex."
msgstr "Хорошо, потому что есть вопрос твоего... пола."

#. emotion: Nervously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Good, but first, before your lesson, I think you've been on good behavior."
msgstr "Хорошо, но сначала, перед твоим уроком, я думаю, ты хорошо себя вела."

#. emotion: Confidently assured
msgctxt "speaker:Man"
msgid "Good, cause that also means whatever she do, that's on you."
msgstr "Хорошо, потому что это значит — что бы она ни сделала, ответишь ты."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "Good, cause the easiest way to get through it is to just go along with it."
msgstr "Хорошо, потому что самый лёгкий способ пройти через это — просто согласиться."

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Master"
msgid "Good, child."
msgstr "Хорошо, дитя."

#. emotion: Sincerely apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "Good, for I mean no offense by it."
msgstr "Хорошо, я вовсе не хотел обидеть тебя."

#. emotion: Calmly approving
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Good, good."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо."

#. emotion: Calmly approving
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, good."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо."

#. emotion: Calmly approving
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Good, good."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо."

#. emotion: Calmly approving
msgctxt "speaker:Jaeid"
msgid "Good, good."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Good, good. Can't wait to leave this horrid place behind me."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо. Не могу дождаться, когда покину это ужасное место."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Good, good. Daemonology is dangerous stuff. You're a decent study, but you're far from ready to start practicing on your own."
msgstr "Хорошо, хорошо. Демонология — опасная штука. Ты неплохо учишься, но ты далеко не готова практиковать самостоятельно."

#. emotion: Casually content
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good, how for a start, some food and drinks for me and my friend here."
msgstr "Отлично, для начала — еда и выпивка для меня и моей подруги."

#. emotion: Encouragingly with a smile
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, let's get to practicin then."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда давай приступим к практике."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Good, now I got to get back to keepin this ship runnin."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь мне нужно вернуться к управлению кораблём."

#. emotion: With confident self-assurance
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, now I'm already hard as a rock, so I ain't gonna waste it."
msgstr "Хорошо, а я уже твёрдый как камень, так что не собираюсь это тратить впустую."

#. emotion: Softly apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Tailor"
msgid "Good, now apologize the proper way."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь извинись как следует."

#. emotion: Calmly encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, now can you get some sleep?"
msgstr "Хорошо, теперь ты можешь поспать?"

#. emotion: "With a touch of impatience"
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, now get me my map. I have work to do."
msgstr "Хорошо, теперь принеси мне карту. У меня есть дела."

#. emotion: Commandingly raising voice
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good, now get up here."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь поднимайся сюда."

#. emotion: Calmly directing
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good, now go down the hall, fourth door on the right, report to the tailor."
msgstr "Хорошо, теперь иди по коридору, четвёртая дверь направо, к портному."

#. emotion: In a stern, dismissive tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, now go."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь убирайся."

#. emotion: Neutrally instructive
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, now go. You can work out the details on the loan with the quartermaster."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь идите. Вы можете обсудить детали займа с казначеем."

#. emotion: Suspiciously cautious
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, now hold on to something, cause I wanna break you in tonight."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь держись за что-нибудь, потому что сегодня я хочу как следует тебя отыметь."

#. emotion: Neutral attentively
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good, now listen..."
msgstr "Хорошо, теперь слушай..."

#. emotion: Sincerely apologetic
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Good, now really apologize."
msgstr "Хорошо, теперь извинись по-настоящему."

#. emotion: Casually, with slight curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good, now show me your hands."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь покажи руки."

#. emotion: Motivational encouragement, with a tinge of impatience
msgctxt "speaker:Sakar"
msgid "Good, now stop dreaming and work that cock."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь хватит мечтать, работай над членом."

#. emotion: In a tired but firm tone
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, now stop wasting time and go get some sleep."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь хватит тратить время, иди спать."

#. emotion: In a tired, gentle manner
msgctxt "speaker:Captain"
msgid "Good, now try and reserve your strength."
msgstr "Хорошо, а теперь прибереги силы."

#. emotion: Contemplatively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Good, she thought, as she could already feel her thoughts of Xan recede."
msgstr "«Отлично», — подумала она, чувствуя, как мысли о Ксане уже отступают."

#. emotion: Admiringly condescending
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good, so at least we're clear that I save you from your own stupidity."
msgstr "Хорошо, хотя бы мы прояснили, что я спас тебя от твоей же глупости."

#. emotion: Calmly instructive
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Good, take em back and give a nice meal and a warm bath."
msgstr "Хорошо, отведите их обратно и дайте хорошую еду и тёплую ванну."

#. emotion: Contentedly satisfied
msgctxt "speaker:Samayra"
msgid "Good, that's all I ever wanted."
msgstr "Хорошо, это всё, чего я хотела."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, that's my girl."
msgstr "Хорошо, вот моя девочка."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "Good, that's what I like to hear."
msgstr "Хорошо, это я люблю слышать."

#. emotion: Calmly, but with restrained annoyance
msgctxt "speaker:Thomas"
msgid "Good, then I will waste no more of your time."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда я не буду больше тратить твоё время."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Good, then apologize for giving me those angry eyes."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда извинись за то, что смотрела на меня злым взглядом."

#. emotion: In a dismissive, almost scolding tone
msgctxt "speaker:Carolyn"
msgid "Good, then go. You're a smart girl, go solve all your problems."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда иди. Ты умная девочка, иди решай все свои проблемы."

#. emotion: Dismissively confident
msgctxt "speaker:Soldier"
msgid "Good, then if you ain't got nothing to hide, let's get this over with."
msgstr "Хорошо, раз тебе нечего скрывать, давай покончим с этим."

#. emotion: Confidently encouraging
msgctxt "speaker:Gilead"
msgid "Good, then keep up."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда не отставай."

#. emotion: In a confident, clear tone
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Good, then let's be honest."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда будем честны."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, then let's go teach this mutinous fuck a lesson."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда пойдём проучим этого мятежного ублюдка."

#. emotion: Confused, curious whisper
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, then tell me why you are here. Why I am here."
msgstr "Хорошо, тогда скажи мне, почему ты здесь. Почему я здесь."

#. emotion: Confidently affirmed
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good, then we have an understanding."
msgstr "Хорошо, значит, мы договорились."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Matthew"
msgid "Good, turn around and face me, inmate."
msgstr "Хорошо, повернись и смотри на меня, заключённая."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Xanthippe"
msgid "Good, we'll need our sleep for what comes tomorrow. We'll speak before I leave for the gate, I promise."
msgstr "Хорошо, нам понадобится сон перед завтрашним днём. Мы поговорим перед тем, как я уйду к воротам, обещаю."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good, what do you have to report?"
msgstr "Хорошо, что у тебя для доклада?"

#. emotion: Encouragingly, with pride
msgctxt "speaker:Master"
msgid "Good, you are learning."
msgstr "Хорошо, ты учишься."

#. emotion: Confidently, reassuringly
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Good, you don't wanna get involved with that fella, Sarah."
msgstr "Молодец, не стоит связываться с этим парнем, Сара."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Good, you're here."
msgstr "Хорошо, ты здесь."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good, you're learning. I'll make a good ship whore out of you yet."
msgstr "Хорошо, ты учишься. Я ещё сделаю из тебя отличную корабельную шлюху."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Albert"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Alfred"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Eula"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Gorak"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Guard Captain"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Hassar"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Hugh"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Kate"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Kim"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Marion"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Marius"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Metis"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Naydeen"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Vaelen"
msgid "Good."
msgstr "Добро."

#. emotion: In a warm, promising tone
msgctxt "speaker:Captain Belmont"
msgid "Good. After we get married, I'll buy you a nice house."
msgstr "Хорошо. После свадьбы я куплю тебе хороший дом."

#. emotion: Confidently, with assurance
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good. And the whole trip is more than a week."
msgstr "Хорошо. А вся поездка займёт больше недели."

#. emotion: In a gentle, inquisitive tone
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Good. And will you behave again?"
msgstr "Хорошо. Будешь хорошо себя вести?"

#. emotion: Cautiously hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Alaric"
msgid "Good. Because we're here."
msgstr "Хорошо. Потому что мы на месте."

#. emotion: Cautiously urgent
msgctxt "speaker:Hecate"
msgid "Good. Best you don't touch it directly. Or get too close."
msgstr "Хорошо. Лучше не прикасайся к нему напрямую. И не подходи слишком близко."

#. emotion: Inquisitively engaged
msgctxt "speaker:Sophia"
msgid "Good. But how about you try for an answer."
msgstr "Хорошо. А как насчёт того, чтобы попробовать найти ответ?"

#. emotion: Instructively neutral
msgctxt "speaker:Atilla"
msgid "Good. Fall back deeper into the line."
msgstr "Хорошо. Отступай глубже в строй."

#. emotion: With a mixture of relief and contentment
msgctxt "speaker:Raza"
msgid "Good. Good."
msgstr "Хорошо. Хорошо."

#. emotion: Contentedly pleased
msgctxt "speaker:Brigand"
msgid "Good. I figured we would work something out."
msgstr "Хорошо. Я так и думал, что мы договоримся."

#. emotion: Tentatively hopeful
msgctxt "speaker:Sigmund"
msgid "Good. I hope you keep your promise."
msgstr "Хорошо. Надеюсь, ты сдержишь обещание."

#. emotion: Cautiously optimistic
msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Good. I think I have most of what I need."
msgstr "Хорошо. Думаю, у меня есть почти всё, что нужно."

#. emotion: Neutral observation, with restraint
msgctxt "speaker:Daemon"
msgid "Good. I will let this defiance slide. But do not test my temper."
