msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to reason to herself, but before she can dissapear into her own mind, more wax is poured onto her, renewing the burning pain."
msgstr "Сара пытается образумить себя, но прежде чем она успевает исчезнуть в своих мыслях, на неё выливают ещё воска, возобновляя жгучую боль."

#. emotion: Empathetic concern
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to remember the week since her father's death."
msgstr "Сара пытается вспомнить неделю после смерти отца."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to stammer some words as she backs up to the door."
msgstr "Сара пытается что-то промямлить, пятясь к двери."

#. emotion: In a surprised gasp
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to stand, but the second she does, she feels a sharp pain shoot through her right ankle."
msgstr "Сара пытается встать, но как только встаёт, чувствует острую боль в правой лодыжке."

#. emotion: Determinedly, yet hopelessly defiant
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to struggle, but against the titantic strength of these men, she's powerless. They spread out and hold down her legs."
msgstr "Сара пытается сопротивляться, но против титанической силы этих мужчин она бессильна. Они раздвигаются и удерживают её ноги."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tries to touch Kate, comfort her, but she sees Kate retreat from her touch."
msgstr "Сара пытается коснуться Кейт, утешить её, но видит, как Кейт отстраняется от прикосновения."

#. emotion: Surprised and confused
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah tripped over her own words as she tried to search her mind for an answer that made sense to herself."
msgstr "Сара споткнулась о собственные слова, пытаясь найти в голове ответ, который имел бы для неё смысл."

#. emotion: Determinedly fighting uphill
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah trudged up a hill, her boots sinking deep into the sand with each step."
msgstr "Сара с трудом взбиралась на холм, её сапоги с каждым шагом глубоко увязали в песке."

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned about and swiftly locked the door."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и быстро заперла дверь."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned ahead and kept running."
msgstr "Сара повернулась вперёд и продолжила бежать."

#. emotion: Sorrowfully withdrawing, with a sense of despair
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and buried her face into the mattress, muffling her screams."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась и уткнулась лицом в матрас, заглушая крики."

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and left the tent."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и вышла из шатра."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and left, taking off down another hallway."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и ушла, направившись по другому коридору."

#. emotion: In a playful and mischievous tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and left."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и вышла."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and looked at the woman."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и посмотрела на женщину."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and moved for the exit."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и направилась к выходу."

#. emotion: Calmly observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and quickly walked away."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и быстро ушла."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and ran out of the cave."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и выбежала из пещеры."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and ran."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и побежала."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw Alaric standing near a woman."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела Аларика, стоящего рядом с женщиной."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw Jasmine standing on the opposite side of the room."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела Жасмин, стоящую на противоположной стороне комнаты."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw Marius walking up the road."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела Мариуса, идущего по дороге."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw Samayra's stern face."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела суровое лицо Самайры."

#. emotion: In awe, quietly amazed
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw countless soldiers. Her soldiers. Rushing up to her, joyous screams!"
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела бесчисленных солдат. Её солдат. Они бежали к ней с радостными криками!"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and saw the thin strap of leather run between her ass cheeks."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и увидела тонкий кожаный ремешок между ягодицами."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and stormed off."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и вышла."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and took her leave."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и ушла."

#. emotion: In a calm, gentle manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and walked away."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и ушла."

#. emotion: With relief, contentedly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and walked back into the cafe, leaving Alaric by himself in the alley."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и пошла обратно в кафе, оставив Аларика одного в переулке."

#. emotion: Warily intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and walked out of the cave."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и вышла из пещеры."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned and watched a woman, dragged along by the hem of her shirt, a soldier pulling her violently."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела женщину, которую тащили за подол рубашки — солдат сильно её тянул."

#. emotion: Anxiously scanning
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around again and again in every direction. The cart was gone. As were the men."
msgstr "Сара оборачивалась снова и снова во все стороны. Повозка исчезла. Как и люди."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and began to walk up the side of the dune."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и пошла вверх по склону дюны."

#. emotion: Surprised and curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and looked at her."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и посмотрела на неё."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and looked at him."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и посмотрела на него."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and looked back at the stage."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и посмотрела назад, на сцену."

#. emotion: With a mixture of surprise and curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and saw Alaric's face in the shadow."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела в тени лицо Аларика."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and she could see the ridge above her."
msgstr "Сара обернулась и увидела гребень над собой."

#. emotion: Surprised and excited
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and stormed off the ship, running straight back to the mercenary camp."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и выбежала с корабля, помчавшись прямо обратно в лагерь наёмников."

#. emotion: Nervously cautious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and walked back into the tent, the only place in the world she still felt somewhat safe."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и вернулась в палатку — единственное место в мире, где она всё ещё чувствовала себя хоть немного в безопасности."

#. emotion: Calmly curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around and walked back to the door."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и пошла обратно к двери."

#. emotion: Surprised, hesitant
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around in shock and saw one of the guards from the auction house standing there. She tried to cover up, but naked and straddling the old soldier with nowhere to go, she only embarrassed herself further."
msgstr "Сара в шоке обернулась и увидела одного из стражников аукционного дома. Она попыталась прикрыться, но голая и верхом на старом солдате, без возможности скрыться, она только ещё больше смутилась."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around to face Thomas."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, чтобы посмотреть на Томаса."

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around to her soldiers."
msgstr "Сара повернулась к своим солдатам."

#. emotion: With a mix of surprise and urgency
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around to leave."
msgstr "Сара развернулась, чтобы уйти."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around to walk out of the alley."
msgstr "Сара повернулась, чтобы выйти из переулка."

#. emotion: In a detached, mildly amused manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around, but she saw no traces of the thing anywhere."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, но не увидела никаких следов этой штуки."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around, facing him, a playful smile on her face."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, глядя на него, с игривой улыбкой на лице."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around, looking out across the Grand Hall."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, оглядывая Большой Зал."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around, now pressing her breasts up against the old soldier's chest."
msgstr "Сара повернулась, прижимаясь грудью к груди старого солдата."

#. emotion: Startled curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around, shocked by the sudden voice."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, потрясённая внезапным голосом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around."
msgstr "Сара обернулась."

#. emotion: Reflective astonishment
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around. Her eyes saw, but she didn't understand. It took her a moment to process what she was seeing."
msgstr "Сара обернулась. Её глаза видели, но она не понимала. Потребовалось мгновение, чтобы осознать увиденное."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around. She was alone."
msgstr "Сара обернулась. Она была одна."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned around?"
msgstr "Сара обернулась?"

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned as she suddenly saw her brother approach."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, когда внезапно увидела приближающегося брата."

#. emotion: Anxiously worried
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away and continued to run."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась и побежала дальше."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away and continued to walk down the hall of the western wing, the screams of the woman slowly fading away behind her."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась и продолжила идти по коридору западного крыла, крики женщины постепенно затихали у неё за спиной."

#. emotion: Casually indifferent
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away and slowly walked towards Damian."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась и медленно пошла к Дамиану."

#. emotion: Neutrally admiring
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away from the great building towards Kate's voice."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась от величественного здания на голос Кейт."

#. emotion: In a defensive, hurt tone
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away, resenting the compliment."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась, обиженная этим комплиментом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away, staring out into the brush."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась, уставившись в кусты."

#. emotion: Warily observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away, too awkward to face the girl."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась, слишком смущённая, чтобы смотреть на девушку."

#. emotion: Calmly detached
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned away."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back and faced Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Сара повернулась и посмотрела на леди Кэролин."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around and started fiddling with the clothes."
msgstr "Сара развернулась и начала возиться с одеждой."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around to face Lady Carolyn."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, чтобы встретиться лицом с леди Кэролин."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around to face Sigmund."
msgstr "Сара развернулась, чтобы посмотреть на Сигмунда."

#. emotion: Attentively observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around to face Xan."
msgstr "Сара обернулась обратно к Ксану."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around to him."
msgstr "Сара снова повернулась к нему."

#. emotion: Calmly and reassuringly
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back around."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to face Alaric."
msgstr "Сара обернулась к Аларику."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to face captain Belmont."
msgstr "Сара повернулась к капитану Бельмонту."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to face him."
msgstr "Сара снова повернулась к нему."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to look at the official."
msgstr "Сара обернулась, чтобы посмотреть на чиновника."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to the door to the room and called out to the girl."
msgstr "Сара повернулась к двери и позвала девушку."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to the fortress."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно к крепости."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to the man who called himself Metis."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно к мужчине, назвавшемуся Метисом."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back to the view of the city, hoping to let the moment be ignored and forgotten."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно к виду на город, надеясь, что этот момент проигнорируют и забудут."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back towards Razaphel."
msgstr "Сара снова повернулась к Разафелю."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back towards the door that supposedly lead to the city. Nauyziri."
msgstr "Сара повернулась к двери, которая, как считалось, вела в город. Науйзири."

#. emotion: Calm curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back towards the gate that lead into the western wing."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно к воротам, ведущим в западное крыло."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back towards the water and slowly waded in."
msgstr "Сара повернула обратно к воде и медленно вошла."

#. emotion: In a reflective, contemplative manner
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back towards the window, continuing to observe the movements of the city."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно к окну, продолжая наблюдать за движением города."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned back, facing the advancing abomination."
msgstr "Сара повернулась обратно, встречая надвигающееся отродье."

#. emotion: Warily, with cautious hope
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned down another another alley, heading deeper into the slums."
msgstr "Сара свернула в очередной переулок, направляясь глубже в трущобы."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned down the direction where the foodstuffs were usually kept, but to her surprise found only more packs of soldiers, busily working."
msgstr "Сара направилась туда, где обычно хранили припасы, но, к своему удивлению, обнаружила там лишь группы солдат, занятых работой."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her attention towards both, but making it clear she spoke on her brother's behalf."
msgstr "Сара обратила внимание на обоих, но давая понять, что говорит от имени брата."

#. emotion: Somberly skeptical
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her body to the side, hoping to deny him much more of a view."
msgstr "Сара повернулась боком, надеясь лишить его дальнейшего обзора."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes away from the sight."
msgstr "Сара отвела взгляд от этого зрелища."

#. emotion: Anxiously hoping
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes back to the ground, hoping to avoid his wrath a second time."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза в землю, надеясь избежать его гнева во второй раз."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes back to the peasant girl and the guard."
msgstr "Сара перевела взгляд обратно на крестьянскую девушку и стражника."

#. emotion: Sternly regretful
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes down the ground."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза к земле."

#. emotion: Softly, with sorrow
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes down towards the ground."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза."

#. emotion: Softly concerned
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes down."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза."

#. emotion: Warily curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes down. Why did she try to defy him when she knew it always ended like this."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза. Зачем она пытается перечить ему, если знает, что это всегда кончается так."

#. emotion: Softly curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes low."
msgstr "Сара опустила глаза."

#. emotion: Cautiously intrigued
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes towards the girl."
msgstr "Сара перевела взгляд на девушку."

#. emotion: Casually glancing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes towards the two men in the circle."
msgstr "Сара перевела взгляд на двух мужчин в круге."

#. emotion: Admiringly curious
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes up to the captain who looked down on her as she continued her efforts."
msgstr "Сара подняла глаза на капитана, который смотрел на неё сверху вниз, пока она продолжала свои старания."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her eyes up towards the Khan and gave her most submissive look."
msgstr "Сара подняла глаза на Хана и сделала самый покорный взгляд."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her face up and looked at him."
msgstr "Сара подняла лицо и посмотрела на него."

#. emotion: Neutral observation
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her hands back over."
msgstr "Сара перевернула руки обратно."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head and looked deep into her eyes."
msgstr "Сара повернула голову и посмотрела глубоко в её глаза."

#. emotion: Surprised curiosity
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head and observed the man. Nothing about him suggested he had ever considered saving a single coin on himself."
msgstr "Сара повернула голову и наблюдала за мужчиной. Ничто в нём не указывало, что он когда-либо считал нужным экономить."

#. emotion: Warmly, with affection
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head and saw Samayra in the crowd."
msgstr "Сара повернула голову и увидела в толпе Самайру."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head at him."
msgstr "Сара повернула голову к нему."

#. emotion: Disinterestedly scanning the room
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head away from the scenes, fixing her eyes on Jaeid again."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась от этих сцен, снова уставившись на Джаида."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head away, staring at the floor."
msgstr "Сара отвернулась, уставившись в пол."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head slowly."
msgstr "Сара медленно повернула голову."

#. emotion: Curiously observing
msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah turned her head to look at the man. A rather large and fat, but seemingly very happy, man stood out in the center of the room."
